<!--Post: 6460--><!--Time: 1107806421-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6460"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 12:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->On the famous 911 tape, he pronounced homicide as HOMEicide with emphasis on O and says the word Park as a New Englander would say paahhk. <BR> <BR>My guess is that he is not originally from the Wichita area and may have moved there around age 21 as speculated in FBI profile. Moving to Wichita MAY have been the separation the agent working up the profile talked about...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6460-->
<!--Post: 6471--><!--Time: 1107809508-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6471"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lazysean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lazysean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 12:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->At no point in the released version of that tape does he say the word &#34;Park&#34;.  If you have access to a longer uneditted version, please share it!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6471-->
<!--Post: 6473--><!--Time: 1107809957-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6473"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 12:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->my apologies lazysean, I mistook Fox for Park. However, it DOES till have that very familiar New England ring I am so very familiar with. Fox or park, the &#39;ahhh&#39; is there. <BR> <BR> <BR>Apologies for the mistake<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6473-->
<!--Post: 6475--><!--Time: 1107811873-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6475"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 1:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree witchking. I also knew a dude in the army who also talked like that. Around Boston area.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6475-->
<!--Post: 6482--><!--Time: 1107819181-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6482"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 3:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->His voice does appear to have a northern tone to it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6482-->
<!--Post: 6617--><!--Time: 1107910629-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6617"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:blingbling1169@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cawichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cawichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 4:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh my goodness Witchking. Just this morning I was in the shower and what did I see on the bottle of baby shampoo? None other than Skillman New Jersey. You remember Bill S. Killman! I was like Whoa! I have been working this lead all day and trying to make sense of it. Do you think he may be from the east coast and was stationed here in the military and knew the Oteros this way&#40; Charlie believes this is how his dad knew BTK&#41;. Or of course this could be a dead end, but that whole park thing just got me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6617-->
<!--Post: 6635--><!--Time: 1107921465-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6635"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 7:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sounds exactly like a guy I know who lives in CA but was born and raised in Minnesota. Isn&#39;t there an existing thread for this subject?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6635-->
<!--Post: 6638--><!--Time: 1107923281-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6638"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 8:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Joseph was stationed in the Panama Canal Zone - and traveled for weeks/months at a time to other places &#40;per Charlie&#41; in the 6 years before moving to Wichita. They had only been in Wichita 4 months or so. In fact, their furniture and personal belongings had just arrived in the weeks before the murders. Its all documented...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6638-->
<!--Post: 6930--><!--Time: 1108080585-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6930"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 4:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was in the Panama CZ before it was turned over to the Panamanians. I remember there were a few installations on the Pacific side, which included Fort Clayton and Howard AFB. I&#39;m sure that if Mr. Otero was stationed there dealing with aircrafts, he would have been stationed at Howard. But, if he flew with the Army, then in Fort Kobbe, or Albrook Field &#40;way back in the 70s&#41;.  <BR> <BR>Well, most everyone working for the Army there got processed and lived in Fort Clayton because it had more housing units. In Fort Clayton there was a building which was #419. It was a hub - it was the post hospital, and beside it there were other big buildings, like the shoppette, the central issue facility, a cafeteria, records clearing, the mess hall, etc... There was a temporary lodging &#40;motel&#41; next to it, too. My point being... what could&#39;ve been building #408 in Clayton. Would be nice to know if the address on BTK&#39;s card had anything to do with that.  <BR> <BR>Probably not, because it&#39;s very possibly one of those things he uses to stumble people. But, being that the Oteros had been there before he retired, maybe it does have something to do with it. <BR> <BR>If anyone remembers or finds out what was in #408, let it be known, please? <BR> <BR><IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6930-->
<!--Post: 7182--><!--Time: 1108263989-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7182"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 7:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ooops! <BR> <BR>That should&#39;ve been building #519... not #419. <BR> <BR><IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7182-->
<!--Post: 7223--><!--Time: 1108305775-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7223"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 6:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom- I know this is off-topic, but I wanted to respond to Ztargate&#39;s post. <BR> <BR>Ztargate- I think you&#39;ve made an interesting connection. Just to refresh memories, I&#39;ve posted the return address BTK used.  <BR> <BR>May 5, 2004: KAKE-TV receives an envelope with a return address of: <BR> <BR>Thomas B. King <BR>408 Clayton Street <BR>Wichita <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll repeat Ztargate&#39;s request: <BR> <BR>If anyone remembers or finds out what was in #408, let it be known, please? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7223-->
<!--Post: 7284--><!--Time: 1108359488-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7284"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 9:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Essevi <BR>Ztargate <BR> <BR>When the letter was published I checked district court property records; there is no listing for 408 Clayton. <BR> <BR>I drove by, there was no property with that street address, no vacant lot etc. <BR> <BR>I went to a title company in Wichita and did a manual check of titles in the 400 block of Clayton. <BR> <BR>408 Clayton has never existed as an address, and no deed has ever been registered with that as the &#34;common&#34; or street address. <BR> <BR>It could be a duplex where the lot is 406 Clayton and the duplex is 406/408 Clayton.  But it&#39;s not. <BR> <BR>It&#39;s not uncommon for a property owner to convert a garage to a rental unit, and the utility companies and post office give it an address that does not show up in a title search.  However, those are a &#34;1/2&#34; address to show a sub-divided main address.  &#40;Example 406 Clayton converts/rents his garaqe, the garage address is 406 1/2 Clayton, not 408 Clayton.&#41; That has not happened either. <BR> <BR>Another possible scenario is that the owner of the lot for 406 Clayton also owned the neighboring lot and used them both for one home. That would have showed up in the title company and court records.  That didn&#39;t happen either. <BR> <BR>There is nothing there physically and nothing in the records. <BR> <BR>How does BTK find addresses that don&#39;t exist? <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7284-->
<!--Post: 7285--><!--Time: 1108359944-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7285"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 9:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ztargate <BR> <BR>There wouldn&#39;t have perchance been a building #440, would there?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7285-->
<!--Post: 7305--><!--Time: 1108387166-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7305"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 5:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ztargate, Whoisbtk and Bmodule <BR> <BR>I think we need to start a thread titled: <BR>  <BR><b>&#34;How does BTK find addresses that don&#39;t exist?&#34;</b> &#40;great title, Whois&#41; <BR> <BR>This seems to be a subject that needs to be explored.  <BR> <BR>Tom- since this has become a most interesting topic located in the wrong thread, is it possible for you to move the last 6 posts into a newly created thread?  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7305-->
